#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This Procedure demonstrates how to use Events to change the Powertrain of the vehicle.
#
#Studying the Powertrain data linked on the Vehicle: Assembly screen, you will see that the truck has rear-wheel drive and an open differential.
#
#As the truck climbs the hill in this test, it gets stuck and starts to roll down the hill.
#
#Using the Events, we are able to monitor when this happens, apply the brakes, and change the powertrain dataset to one with four-wheel drive, a locked transfer case, and locked differentials.
#
#At this point the truck resumes its climb up the hill, this time successfully.
#
#To see how this was set up, click on the Events dataset "A. Get Stuck."
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Procedures; { Event Triggered Tests } 2WD to 4WD
